A||||2||85seNUT||Why wont it start?||||13||
Z||000000||85seNUT||02-02-2001||12:58 AM||||Every once in a while my car just wont start.  After i push start it its usually good for about 2 or 3 times.  then it just wont start.  I dont think it is the starter cuz it doesnt even try to start.  i think it may be the clutch.  maybe the setting is wrong and when i  push it in it doesnt think its in all the way.  i dunno.  anyone have this problem?||||reg||13
Z||000001||JohnnyK||02-02-2001||01:18 AM||||Well, lets try to narrow it down a bit. If you push in the clutch and try to start it, do you hear a click from behind you? If you do, it is either the battery, (charging system), or the starter. If you don't hear a click, and the temp guage pegs itself without any other indication, then your neutral start switch isn't working (switch that knows if the clutch is pushed in all the way). I don't know, but I assume jump starting would start the car with either problem.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||02-02-2001||10:20 AM||||Sounds like the switch at the top of the clutch pedal. Also original Fiero clutch pedals tended to bend with age. You could get a new switch then go to a dealer or FieroShop and get a steel pedal.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
